            <ArticleTitle>[The effect of emotional-pain stress on the activity of carboxypeptidase N--the enzyme of neuropeptide processing in the rat brain].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>23-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Activity of carboxypeptidase N [correction of H] increased under emotional-algic stress in the rat pituitary gland and hypothalamus. Carboxypeptidase N [correction of H] seems to be involved in development of the stress response, and soluble forms of the enzyme take part in processing of secretory peptides. Membrane-bound forms take part in processing of the neuropeptides specific by their central action.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
